advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          search_sources
description   "Search theory source files by regex or literal
              pattern, returning {theory, line, snippet} hits. By
              default searches the base image's sessions plus the
              sessions owning loaded or scoped theories; pass
              `sessions` (glob list) to widen — e.g.
              [\"HOL-Library\"] or [\"*\"] for everything known.
              This is TEXT search over files: it sees theories no
              semantic tool can (unloaded sessions, the AFP), and it
              is how you discover where a constant or lemma lives
              before deciding to load_theory it. Results are capped
              (default 40); narrow the pattern or sessions when
              truncated."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "pattern": {"type": "string"},
                 "sessions": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
                 "max_results": {"type": "integer", "default": 40}},
               "required": ["pattern"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}
              (reads only files the session structure names; still
              openWorld false.)
outputSchema  none.

name/argument mapping across the layers
---------------------------------------

  mcp client edge   tools/call "search_sources",
                    {"pattern": "multiset", "sessions": ["HOL-Library"]}
  scala builtin row resolve sessions -> theory source paths via D1's
                    path map; stream-grep each file, collecting up to
                    max_results (theory long name, 1-based line,
                    trimmed snippet); no bridge, no engine.

